12. Create the Initial API Endpoint
The next step is to expose document generation through the backend.

Example:

from fastapi import FastAPI
from pydantic import BaseModel

from app.services.ai.gemini_service import generate_legal_document

app = FastAPI()


class DocumentRequest(BaseModel):
    document_type: str
    party_a: str
    party_b: str
    effective_date: str
    terms: str


@app.post("/api/documents/generate")
def generate_document(request: DocumentRequest):

    prompt = f"""
    Generate a {request.document_type}.

    Party A: {request.party_a}
    Party B: {request.party_b}
    Effective Date: {request.effective_date}

    Terms:
    {request.terms}

    Generate a professionally structured document
    with appropriate sections and clauses.
    """

    document = generate_legal_document(prompt)

    return {
        "document_type": request.document_type,
        "content": document
    }

This establishes the basic:

Frontend
   ↓
POST /api/documents/generate
   ↓
FastAPI
   ↓
Gemini 2.5 Pro
   ↓
Generated Document

